                <pb facs="0273" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg167"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September 26,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan is instructed to report to the Department the names of the refugees in
                    his legation and the offices they have filled, the crimes they are accused of,
                    and whether process from any regular tribunal has issued against them. He is
                    also directed to report the conduct of the ministers of other countries, whether
                    persons have taken refuge in their legations, and, if so, the action of the
                    Chilean Government respecting them; and to promptly and fully inform the
                    Department of all facts.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
